events A and B are independent if P(A intersection B) = P(A)P(B) = P(A,B)  ( if A occurs we know nothing of about B)

This is completly different from disjointsness ( which means if A occured then B cannot occur)

if A,B,C are independent then P(A,B) = P(A)P(B), P(C,B) = P(B)P(C), P(A,C) = P(A)P(C) and P(A,B,C) = P(A)P(B)P(C)

